  2680                                  ; dev_init_list member, POST 66h. CR0 |= CD|NW, INVD; chipset reg 2 |= 103h, reg 2 &= ~13h, reg 1 |= 103h open the SMRAM window (6000:8000 and 3000:8000 alias the same RAM; SMBASE starts at 30000h so the SMI entry is 3000:8000); writes a far jmp to smi_handler_first there; reg 1 |= F0h (SMI enable, best guess) and reg 6 bit 12 (software SMI trigger) fire two SMIs until the handler has cleared the jmp byte; POST 88h. Afterwards SMBASE = 60000h and the state-save template for std_rsm_cpu_reset lies at 6000:9000.
